THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

CoreLink Workspaces statically links third-party open-source components, each
distributed under its own permissive license (Apache-2.0, MIT, the BSD family,
ISC, Unicode-3.0, CDLA-Permissive-2.0, Zlib, and equivalents). Those licenses
and their copyright/attribution notices are reproduced in the per-release
third-party attribution bundle.

That attribution bundle is GENERATED, not hand-maintained. It is produced with
cargo-about from the workspace's about.toml configuration:

    cargo about generate about.hbs > THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md

The accepted-license allow-list in about.toml is kept consistent with the
[licenses] allow-list in deny.toml (single source of truth: see the note in
deny.toml). Regenerate the bundle whenever the dependency graph changes.
